{"id": "12th_tamil_u3_q454", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "12", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "unit_3", "lesson_id": "kambaramayanam_u3", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "rama_philosophical_dialogue", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "‘துன்பு உளது எனின் அன்றோ சுகம் உளது!’ என்று துன்பத்தின் இன்றியமையாமையை இராமன் யாரிடம் கூறுகிறான்?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "இலக்குவனிடம்", "B": "குகனிடம்", "C": "சீதையிடம்", "D": "சுக்கிரீவனிடம்"}, "explanation": "காட்டிற்குத் தன்னோடு வருவதாகக் கூறிய குகனிடம், ‘துன்பம் இருந்தால்தான் சுகத்தின் அருமை தெரியும்; நாம் பிரிந்திருப்பது துன்பமல்ல, மீண்டும் இணைவோம்’ என இராமன் ஆறுதல் கூறுகிறான்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "To whom does Rama utter the immortal philosophical consoling line: 'Only when sorrow exists is happiness realized'?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Lakshmana", "B": "Guha (Guhan)", "C": "Sita", "D": "Sugriva"}, "explanation": "Rama consoles Guha using the profound philosophical adage 'Thunbu uladhu enin andro sugam uladhu'."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "B", "accepted_keys": ["B"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "12", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 54, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "12th